# `i <= point[key] - 1`: what bounds the variable is made of a read out of an int32 under one of two names. The other side of a relation is judged by what it is made of, as the value that enters a promise is: the step has room.
# Once only the value itself was looked at: "i++ might not be an int32". Unseen for `point.x - 1`: there the walk has the range by itself.
# f1 = lessOne
